        "type": "text",
        "text": "When a barley seed germinates, gibberellin is released from structure <b>A</b>. Gibberellin diffuses to its target cells located in tissue <b>B</b>. This causes the cells at <b>B</b> to synthesise the enzyme amylase.",
        "source": {
          "qp": 3
        }
      }
    ],
